{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a06ddc2d537a91be8c87a771e1da8e","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder take canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"; echo \"EXIT:$?\""},"partialResult":{"content":[]}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a06ddc2d537a91be8c87a771e1da8e","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder take canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"; echo \"EXIT:$?\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering\",\"title\":\"Zero-instance empty inventory page and fragment rendering lack regression cover\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\",\"repo\":\"misty-step/canopy\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"lease\":{\"agent\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"principal\":\"none\",\"until\":\"2026-09-04T23:19:02.012Z\"},\"ask\":null,\"proof\":null,\"abandoned\":false,\"notes\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T18:58:37.391Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:49 (handlePage), server.go:82 (handleInstance), templates/fleet.html:36, templates/instance.html:145. Behaviors: when Canopy runs with zero configured or discovered instances, GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance must return HTTP 200 and gracefully render the empty-state templates (\\\"No instances configured.\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\", \\\"Add an instance to the inventory to begin observing it.\\\") without panic, nil pointer dereference, or HTTP 500. Failing example: initialize NewApp with Inventory{Instances: []} and issue GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance; today all tests in server_test.go initialize testInventory() with one pre-configured instance, leaving the zero-instance empty template rendering path unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in server_test.go with an empty inventory asserting that GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance return HTTP 200, contain the expected empty-state text (\\\"No instances configured\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\"), and do not produce template execution errors. Observed: templates have explicit branches for empty instances (fleet.html:36, instance.html:145), but grep shows no test in server_test.go exercises an empty App inventory. Required: HTTP handler regression tests for empty-inventory page and fragment rendering. Proposed test-work: add server tests verifying that GET /, /fragments/fleet, and /fragments/instance return 200 with empty-state messages when no instances are configured.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T18:58:32.84Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\n"}],"details":{}}}
