gments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance must return HTTP 200 and gracefully render the empty-state templates (\\\"No instances configured.\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\", \\\"Add an instance to the inventory to begin observing it.\\\") without panic, nil pointer dereference, or HTTP 500. Failing example: initialize NewApp with Inventory{Instances: []} and issue GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance; today all tests in server_test.go initialize testInventory() with one pre-configured instance, leaving the zero-instance empty template rendering path unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in server_test.go with an empty inventory asserting that GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance return HTTP 200, contain the expected empty-state text (\\\"No instances configured\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\"), and do not produce template execution errors. Observed: templates have explicit branches for empty instances (fleet.html:36, instance.html:145), but grep shows no test in server_test.go exercises an empty App inventory. Required: HTTP handler regression tests for empty-inventory page and fragment rendering. Proposed test-work: add server tests verifying that GET /, /fragments/fleet, and /fragments/instance return 200 with empty-state messages when no instances are configured.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T18:58:32.84Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788549542052},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgF-55lHaue3olSkF3YA6j8pCOXDVnyxhlNovf2VgtPaOip6TEuyvEGobYkFcEdT90PnTOzcXZjCMizGn9NYw3HG4l0XGnQHqVuEh9ZESPcN3vsF8vZc4vhYP1Q2ZYzj9ayGWbzP63yjhYIhmb1os_lVQizMn-wrWh8uhrGvTwVnIgJW0BI9VWaOUMen3m7SSsZrB65Q7K-7rLSlyJ4gm2XCnMbNSnJ1VTiULB5k2s8DClozktkiSCZghA4nPL0gQbKhV1kJ6JzU35rTSXvhzd1aCacencnnvKzdRM56xApcc_Qfn6zqlJ_5hR_jlXEo8oeaxIXWZfFi8M9BqwRP1Zx6SPHK79NUWQV2kSkqAqarMOWnFeRumgDkiNM6Rpa-VitwI6bD9pxgQJM6WZ-lkJ-gH-lfiWkixAiqvKuhg3u6KPqpM1LKHgid3kLu1AQdXJfJQMlvI_GTlPAjF3Kbr0oNTRivIqR5_T5wMn7BLIWl0SdUZcKcKJfKHnYkLntt3lghYx3gHptA9JtF5Z4fiwm405Xi2Pdb0vZroV6nZ5SGbfa-F6RDfwDmPmqzp5vatMVvfzhwDyno_J_81z7VDkhljWlcL2vQ23ZwSNs4jTiY8htxI6OgRHVmY7VmIeV84J1o43SDoVJysko4GU4K4OS0LdnwI9lFWRTv9elLG5sSwZiegdAamr4jsB8IxUggvnDxDlj9SQJCoalXpp_CPY5Hl-YKky3uynvWbg-GYRafG4kw21rIgXLstzoeVWU9qC2XeK83P6jvQN9W6Wqy5ftQQgmNCUW6u7R6VrnUdtO8RajeiN4GCvPvU8giM1QxvDn_70YPBw9x2nDNwqsdzPOlZU17wWqz5KJ